// PCI vendor/device/subsystem identifier database for axl-sdk.
//
// Curated subset of the canonical pci.ids registry — focused on
// devices that show up in QEMU emulation, common server/BMC
// hardware, and the consumer workloads axl-sdk consumers actually
// encounter (NICs, NVMe, GPUs). Numeric IDs themselves are
// uncopyrightable factual data; names are sourced from the public
// pci.ids registry (https://pci-ids.ucw.cz/).
//
// Schema 2 — hierarchical: devices nest under their parent vendor;
// subsystems nest under their parent device. Locality of related
// rows is the win when maintaining thousands of entries by hand.
// (Schema 1 was the flat layout — three top-level arrays. The
// loader still accepts schema 1 for backwards compatibility, but
// new files should use schema 2.)
//
// To extract a larger set from the full pci.ids text database,
// see scripts/pci-ids-to-json5.py.
{
    schema: 2,
    vendors: [
        { id: 0x1000, name: 'LSI / Broadcom',
          devices: [
            { did: 0x0097, name: 'MegaRAID SAS 9460-16i' },
          ],
        },
        { id: 0x1002, name: 'AMD / ATI',
